  "strategyNotes": [
    "Construction notices test what residents must DO. Circle every 〜てください and 〜ておいてください.",
    "〜ことがあります after a plain verb means 'may sometimes happen', not 'has happened'. The brown water is a possibility.",
    "場合 (case) introduces a conditional exception: 雨の場合 = if it rains. Expect a question on it."
